>>
Rule 1 (input must be floating-point to avoid unsupported complex/integer types)
{v_1 : tensor} |= dtype_(v_1) = 6 ∨ dtype_(v_1) = 7 ∨ dtype_(v_1) = 8
>>
Rule 2 (when out is provided, its dtype must match input to avoid casting errors)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= dtype_(v_2) = dtype_(v_1)
>>
Rule 3 (when out is provided, its shape must match input shape)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= ndim(v_1) = ndim(v_2) ∧ ∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : shape(v_1, i) = shape(v_2, i)
>>
Rule 4 (inputs are within the principal domain of erfinv to ensure well-defined finite outputs)
{v_1 : tensor} |= min(v_1) > -1 ∧ max(v_1) < 1
